{"parentUuid":"6b673f44-8736-4c8a-9a67-ac18ff65d1f9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ada392f8670716699","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_013hZyAhhGsmtw99w8j2EVBU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XJkm5YSYFWiJvdABYyAYow","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/docs/dmitry/theory/fra_paper_tex && grep -n \"fig:retrieval\\|fig6_retrieval\" fra_paper.tex","description":"Check for fig:retrieval label and fig6 inclusion"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":110279,"output_tokens":340,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":705},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":110279,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cbx7fSW8DBLxUE8ZAtEaV","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"57ec0df0-34d1-4af1-8381-2c3fd53d609d","timestamp":"2026-06-11T20:37:43.785Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"57ec0df0-34d1-4af1-8381-2c3fd53d609d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"2c8a0751-1493-4563-8cf9-c724afe36b6d","agentId":"ada392f8670716699","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XJkm5YSYFWiJvdABYyAYow","type":"tool_result","content":"206:Across five behaviors spanning two model families, an FRA cell-edit beats the strongest fair linear baseline by $1$--$4$ orders of magnitude on legit-content KL at matched removal (Table~\\ref{tab:wins}, Figs.~\\ref{fig:sprint2},~\\ref{fig:retrieval},~\\ref{fig:lbnr}).\n225:\\paragraph{Retrieval is the strongest confirmed win} (Fig.~\\ref{fig:retrieval}). On a Gemma-2-2b associative-retrieval task (``box A holds frog''; query the box, retrieve the value), FRA cuts the (box-query $\\times$ frog-value) pair. It survives every prong of the gauntlet: a clean random-off-edge null does nothing (selected pairs $0.021$ vs.\\ random off-edge $0.213\\approx$ base); at matched removal vs.\\ head-ablation, legit-frog KL is $0.002$ vs.\\ $0.010$; transfer to a new position succeeds where a position-patch fails ($0.261{\\to}0.044$ vs.\\ $0.261{\\to}0.261$). The decisive prong: at matched on-target removal (FRA $0.042$ / steer $0.024$), legit-frog KL is FRA $0.0016$ vs.\\ steer $1.77$---\\textbf{${\\sim}1{,}100\\times$ more separable}. A content-gated linear steer strong enough to suppress retrieval \\emph{destroys the frog representation everywhere frog-content appears}; FRA cuts only the pair. This attributes the advantage to the QK pair structure, not to content-addressing per se.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3cbc8ed3-e666-43f5-9046-bb05bd876c63","timestamp":"2026-06-11T20:37:43.834Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"57ec0df0-34d1-4af1-8381-2c3fd53d609d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"3cbc8ed3-e666-43f5-9046-bb05bd876c63","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ada392f8670716699","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01872zQQk6rewHvs4SmwjeZb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — I reference `fig:retrieval` but never included the `fig6_retrieval.png` figure. I have that figure copied and a good caption from viewing it. Let me add it right after the retrieval paragraph."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":903,"cache_read_input_tokens":110984,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":903,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cbx7ftwMkVboRPULCZAKd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4dd10f4-2f74-40ae-a79e-8b0807566128","timestamp":"2026-06-11T20:37:47.300Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"e4dd10f4-2f74-40ae-a79e-8b0807566128","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ada392f8670716699","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01872zQQk6rewHvs4SmwjeZb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TdEckuwaq69GT6tB3WxefC","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/docs/dmitry/theory/fra_paper_tex/fra_paper.tex","old_string":"A content-gated linear steer strong enough to suppress retrieval \\emph{destroys the frog representation everywhere frog-content appears}; FRA cuts only the pair. This attributes the advantage to the QK pair structure, not to content-addressing per se.","new_string":"A content-gated linear steer strong enough to suppress retrieval \\emph{destroys the frog representation everywhere frog-content appears}; FRA cuts only the pair. This attributes the advantage to the QK pair structure, not to content-addressing per se.\n\n\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{fig6_retrieval.png}\n\\caption{\\textbf{A real-world FRA win: controlling long-context retrieval} (Gemma-2-2b + GemmaScope). $P(\\text{``frog''})$ retrieved under three operating conditions; FRA is the only method that is \\emph{both} separable and transferable. \\emph{(1) Remove the retrieval}: FRA-QK ($0.02$) and the attention-patch ($0.03$) both suppress; content-suppress also kills it ($0.00$). \\emph{(2) Preserve ``frog'' in a legit context} (want HIGH): FRA keeps it ($0.15\\approx$ baseline $0.16$); content-suppress \\emph{destroys legit ``frog''} ($0.00$). \\emph{(3) Transfer: remove on a new context} (want LOW): FRA cuts it ($0.03$) while the position-patch \\emph{fails to transfer} ($0.47\\approx$ baseline). Only FRA satisfies all three; the decisive legit-content-KL comparison (Definition~\\ref{def:metric}) against a content-gated steer gives FRA ${\\sim}1{,}100\\times$ lower collateral at matched removal.}\n\\label{fig:retrieval}\n\\end{figure}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":903,"cache_read_input_tokens":110984,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":903,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cbx7ftwMkVboRPULCZAKd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3bfe5a0e-59b4-4063-8beb-964c1293b2ba","timestamp":"2026-06-11T20:37:56.415Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
