{"parentUuid":"8b4ac19b-0e13-4557-94f6-87d5337ea3b6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ada392f8670716699","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01MNfdQurKXw4Fa3BtTxL4dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Figures render correctly with self-contained captions, citations resolve (the blue hyperlinks work), and cross-references are intact. The paper is complete and polished.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Path to the paper:** `/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/docs/dmitry/theory/fra_paper_tex/fra_paper.tex`\n\n**Compilation:** Compiles cleanly with `pdflatex` (run 3-4 times for refs/TOC). Final output: **15 pages, 0 undefined references, 0 missing figures, 0 errors.** One residual overfull hbox of 1.78pt (sub-visible, in the boundary table) — cosmetically negligible. PDF verified visually (title/abstract/TOC and a figure page render correctly with the same LM-font + blue-link styling as the original `fra.tex`).\n\n**Section list:**\n1. Introduction (motivation, 3 claims, novelty)\n2. Setup: the cell decomposition — exact cell partition `S[q,k]=Σ u^μ_q u^ν_k ω_{μν}`, cell-as-AND, cell-level weight edit, set algebra; **2.1** Nonlinearity ledger (Proposition: RMSNorm scalar / RoPE rotation / Gemma soft-cap = one true nonlinearity / GPT-2 LN artifact)\n3. Theory: score-space expressivity (row/column never a cell) + residual broadcast; Separability-gap proposition; the magnitude-law claim\n4. The predictor: five-clause win-checklist (CCF, LBNR, causal head-finding)\n5. Experiments — **5.1** corrected fair metric (legit-content KL vs content-gated projection-removal steer; why head-ablation/position-patch are strawmen); **5.2** confirmed-wins table (retrieval 1100×, acronym 26,000×, copy-suppression 516×, backdoor 25×, induction 15×); **5.3** magnitude-law curve; **5.4** boundary map table\n6. Related work (Elhage, Olsson, McDougall, Wu, Wang, Garcia-Carrasco, SAEs, ActAdd/CAA/Arditi, Conmy)\n7. Limitations (narrow win-class, Gemma CCF sink-mask, reach ceiling, no ln1 SAE, small N, two model families)\n- **Appendix A:** induction win + sleeper bridge (the existence proof) — Fig. of induction win\n- **Appendix B:** methods/protocol details\n- **Appendix C:** reuse and the corpus-firing-rate failure\n\n**Figures (5, all copied into the folder and `\\includegraphics`'d with self-contained captions):** `fig_sprint2_summary.png` (win/loss map + decisive metric), `fig_magnitude_law.png` (the curve), `fig6_retrieval.png` (separable×transferable 2×2), `fig9_lbnr_tier2.png` (LBNR gate + copy-suppression), `fig1_final.png` (induction, Appendix A).\n\n**Style:** Reused the full preamble/macros from `fra.tex` (documentclass, geometry, fontenc/lmodern/microtype, amsmath/booktabs, blue hyperref, the `\\R \\E \\ip \\softmax \\diag \\OV \\QK \\dhead` macros and the definition/proposition/claim/protocol/remark environments; added `\\reuse` and `graphicx`). Used `natbib` for author-year citations against an inline `thebibliography`.\n\n**Numbers — all pulled from the source docs; none invented.** Two judgment calls worth flagging:\n- The Table 1 caption notes that copy-suppression's headline figure appears two ways in the sources — **516×** (natural-text vs head-ablation, RESULTS_SUMMARY/CAMPAIGN_REPORT) and **22.7×** (the synthetic probe in `fig9`). I reported 516× in the table and noted the 22.7× synthetic-probe value in the figure caption, matching how the figure itself is labeled, to avoid a number mismatch between table and figure.\n- The in-context backdoor \"25×\" (used in `fig_sprint2_summary`) vs the \"~27×\" DoM ratio in `summary.md` — I used **25×** in the table to match the summary figure, and gave the underlying 0.07 vs 1.83 nats so the reader can see the source.\n- Induction's matched-50% baseline is labeled **2.66** in `fig1_final.png` but **2.66 ± 1.35** in the summary text; I used the value with error bars from the text. No numbers were omitted."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequenc